{"id": "EUVD-2026-107373", "enisaUuid": "5b142395-3e20-3ddc-b0f5-8f06713879cf", "description": "Multiple Cisco products are affected by a vulnerability in the Snort 3 Generic Routing Encapsulation (GRE) Detection Engine that could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause the Snort 3 Detection Engine to restart, resulting in an interruption of packet inspection.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to incomplete error checking when Snort 3 parses GRE packets. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted GRE packet to a targeted device to be parsed by Snort. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the Snort 3 Detection Engine to restart unexpectedly, resulting in a DoS condition.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T16:12:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T19:11:03", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-snort3-misc-dos-6mB22qAK"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-20179", "GHSA-9v2c-x8g8-r7m4"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.39, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02ecdd3e-ced4-374f-b47d-e54633db87a7", "product": {"name": "Cisco UTD SNORT IPS Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "17.12.1a"}, {"id": "0499540d-5ced-3983-8317-9b76468cb846", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.9.7.0"}, {"id": "052b0bf2-1bbb-3913-bd14-97c8ca2d1ddd", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.84.0"}, {"id": "052d1ffb-50d5-3b75-9751-de9fd95b9f22", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.70.0"}, {"id": "061d1c4b-f563-3702-8601-ae341b3fd450", "product": {"name": "Cisco Open Source Snort3", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.8.1.0"}, {"id": "06ee5df3-cfdf-3749-9607-1b3f4f15a7a3",